{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested for lane E at exact head 4d8a6f377b8cfc7afb7b298fe4b52a65414c6349. Primary basis: packages/client/README.md; all 59 submitted artifact bases are included. Full functionality remains the review target.\n\nValidation: clean npm installation, repository type checks, 63 client Node tests plus 2 workerd signing tests, 11 CLI tests, and 36 MCP Node tests plus 1 workerd handler test passed. The CLI bundle builds, the built bin answers help, and dry packing includes the bin and bundle. Seven independent diagnostic tests in an isolated checkout reproduce the six findings below; their passing assertions describe the defects, not fixes. Production sources were not changed. The fake Room is useful transport evidence, not evidence of deployed Room/Artifacts integration.\n\n1. [P1, Security] Register an existing bearer before the first authenticated read. In packages/client/src/connect.ts, the bearer branch uses HttpWire.read to obtain genesis before HttpRoomClient adds the bearer to its Redactor. A 401 ArtroomError that includes the supplied bearer therefore escapes unchanged. An independent fetch fixture confirms the thrown message contains the exact token. Register known credentials before any wire operation; cover initial connection failures as well as errors after connection, and ensure the CLI cannot print them. This is a failure of the package's stated defence against echoed credentials, not a claim that the deployed Room deliberately echoes tokens.\n\n2. [P2, Architecture/recovery] Refresh ended read sessions during WebSocket reconnect. packages/client/src/room.ts watch reopens using auth(), which retains its cached session while its advertised TTL has more than a minute left. After the server ends that session early and drops the socket, the client retries the invalid token indefinitely until near expiry. The independent test ends sessions, drops sockets, and produces another act: no connection is restored and no new session is issued. Reauthorize a reconnect when the old session is no longer valid, retain the last cursor, and test recovery and disposal without replaying delivered updates. A permanently revoked bearer must also have a deliberate observable failure path rather than silently retrying forever.\n\n3. [P1, Architecture/durable credentials] Finish login locally before deleting its recovery record. packages/cli/src/main.ts saves the final key and removes the pending join before connecting for genesis/name and writing config. A failure at that lookup leaves a joined member and saved key, but no config or pending record. Repeating the identical invitation command generates another key and returns invitation-invalid; the CLI cannot resume the join it just completed. This is reproduced with GET /log returning a nonretryable 503 after successful join. Retain durable completion state until credential and room config installation finish; resume the same key and receipt across failures or process interruption at each local step. Apply the same completion discipline to a saved room-custody bearer and config installation, without retrying a one-time redemption.\n\n4. [P2, Architecture/idempotency] Preserve the resolved act across CLI retries. packages/cli/src/main.ts propose reads the current lane and substitutes its current generation when --expect is omitted. Run the same command twice with the same explicit --idempotency-key: the first succeeds, and the second sends a different expectedGeneration and receives idempotency-mismatch. The printed retry instructions and generated AGENTS.md promise the original result. Persist the complete resolved act or signed envelope before submitting it and reuse that binding after restart; avoid rebuilding it from a changed HEAD, lane, lease or proposal. Receipt retrieval must not be blocked by preflight checks that only describe current state. Test a lost success response followed by a separate CLI invocation after state has changed.\n\n5. [P2, Simplification/operation continuity] Make the printed landing follow-up observe the accepted operation. After successful artroom land, output says 'Next: artroom land --wait'. That command always submits another land act; while the original is active it returns land-in-progress, rather than waiting. The independent demo-loop fixture reproduces the printed command and refusal. Carry the operation ID durably or accept an explicit operation to wait on, and have the follow-up read/wait that same operation. Keep starting a new attempt distinct and explicit. Test nonwaiting start followed by waiting, timeout followed by resumption, and terminal failure outcomes.\n\n6. [P2, Security/input boundary] Use own-property checks for the MCP tool table and schema properties. In packages/mcp/src/run.ts, 'constructor' satisfies name in TOOLS, then validate(undefined, ...) throws TypeError outside the advertised never-throw result boundary. In packages/mcp/src/validate.ts, an extra JSON 'toString' property resolves through the schema property's prototype and is accepted despite additionalProperties:false. Independent tests confirm both. Require own registered tool names and own declared schema keys, and return structured bad-request errors for malformed input. Cover constructor, __proto__ and other inherited names on both the direct runner and transport boundaries. These are validation and result-shaping defects; no privilege bypass is demonstrated.\n\nArchitecture: sharing RoomApi across HTTPS, RPC, bearer MCP and stdio, and keeping the transport-free tool runner separate, are useful choices. Byte-identical automatic retries and independent signature vectors are strong evidence. Durable local command completion and reconnect authorization are the missing continuity boundaries.\n\nSecurity: nonextractable browser keys, private credential files, token-free URLs and one-time redemption guidance are sound. Complete first-use redaction and own-property validation before relying on those guarantees.\n\nSimplification: retain the ten contract tools and concise command guidance. A single durable CLI act/completion journal and operation-aware wait path should make the instructions true with less user repair work. The CLI package also declares an exports target src/index.ts that does not exist and is not packed; remove that unused library export or provide a real supported entry point.\n\nIntegration follow-up: README accurately limits this candidate to fake-Room transport tests. When contract amendment 2 is adopted, reconcile the RoomWire bearer requests, because passthrough, attention publication point from the same snapshot, and unknown-explain structured shape with that contract and the production Room. No unrequested live deployment is required for this review. Requested lane E behavior is not reduced by schedule estimates.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:9b6bcd230171879cf56993ab7e381418d389d701","binding":"assigned","head":"4d8a6f377b8cfc7afb7b298fe4b52a65414c6349","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e2e56d74b1f3cab1a5465ffff2fa70abf4874d52\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:3f934a98fa8efcc34c1695fee9b59e58568876e3\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e2e56d74b1f3cab1a5465ffff2fa70abf4874d52","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}